[Music]  we can all use some help during our  parenting journey and today we chat with  a prior educator on some tips for  success if you're looking for a strong  support group and a better connection  with your own children  jennifer cervantes was a prior educator  and is currently the founder of tough as  a mother tribe her first tip  be vulnerable with other parents share  how you really feel and what you're  struggling with  being real will help build a strong  support system and help others guide you  with things you may struggle with  her second tip be present with your kids  do something fun together and it doesn't  even have to cost a penny  i remember like not growing up with a  lot of money like but i remember  all the things we did a lot of them were  free and that's going back to public  school teaching  i taught thousands of kids and after  every monday when they would talk about  what they did over the weekend it was  never like  oh look at my new shirt or this  sometimes it was among peers but  you know listening in on for over a  decade kids  always talked about what and we're so  fulfilled with the things that  going fishing going on a picnic that  really meant something to them  the last tip be honest with your kids  talk through key issues that are  happening in your life and around the  world kids are intuitive we often want  to protect them by not sharing  but by knowing what's going on around  them it helps children build a solid  connection with you  and by sharing your feelings your  children will feel safer when they're in  the loop  and when you communicate openly and  honestly with them

